@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title Git identity & context — commits attributable, no host gitconfig mounted

node "Host" as HOST <<host>> {
  component "internal/gitidentity\nResolve(getenv, …) → EnvPairs" as GID <<app>>
  database "explicit GIT_AUTHOR_* env\n(else host ""git config"")" as SRC <<db>>
  folder "~/.gitconfig" as HOSTCFG <<error>>
}

node "Agent container" as CTR <<host>> {
  component "docker run -e GIT_AUTHOR_NAME …\n-e GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL …" as ENVIN <<app>>
  component "bridge_git_identity\n→ GIT_CONFIG_KEY_n / VALUE_n / COUNT" as BRIDGE <<app>>
  component "report_git_context\nrepo? · origin? · identity? · gh auth?" as REPORT <<app>>
  component "git / gh (baked in every image)" as GIT <<app>>
  database "repo-local .git/config" as LOCAL <<db>>
}

SRC ARROW_MAIN GID
GID ARROW_MAIN ENVIN : bare ""-e NAME"" pairs
HOSTCFG ARROW_ERROR CTR : errorLabel(never mounted)
ENVIN ARROW_MAIN BRIDGE
BRIDGE ARROW_MAIN GIT : " ""git config --get user.name"" resolves\nfile-free "
LOCAL ARROW_MAIN GIT : repo-local identity stays authoritative
BRIDGE ARROW_MAIN REPORT
REPORT ARROW_MAIN CTR : startup preamble

note right of BRIDGE
  **Why config-env, not a written file.** Writing a
  ""~/.gitconfig"" inside the container would (a) need a
  home the arbitrary uid owns and (b) leave a file the
  agent can rewrite. ""GIT_CONFIG_KEY_n"" / ""_VALUE_n"" +
  ""GIT_CONFIG_COUNT"" injects the same values for the
  process tree only.

  The bridge is **additive and non-overriding**: it only
  sets keys ""git config --get"" cannot already resolve, so
  a repo that pins its own identity keeps it.

  Like every other env-shaped step, this must run in the
  def's shell — ""prep"" cannot export it
  (_spec/cmd/proveo-entrypoint/prep-process-boundary.puml).
end note

note bottom of REPORT
  The preamble states plainly whether this is a tracked
  repo, whether a remote exists, whose identity commits
  will carry, and whether ""gh"" is authenticated — so an
  agent about to commit or push is never guessing, and a
  human reading the transcript can attribute the work.

  **The host-side header answers the same question, and
  once answered it wrongly.** ""gitRootOrEmpty"" is the
  repository root //regardless of workspace layout//: it
  gates on ""workspace\.Scope\.IsRepo"" and returns the
  resolved repo root. Reading ""wsSpec\.RepoRoot"" instead
  is the bug it replaced — that field is populated only
  for the app layout, so an app harness reported
  a real repository as absent.
end note
note bottom of GID
  **Identity is resolved on the host and forwarded as bare env**, never by
  mounting the developer's git config: the config may reference signing
  keys, credential helpers and include-paths that mean nothing inside the
  container. Explicit ""GIT_AUTHOR_*"" / ""GIT_COMMITTER_*"" win, then the
  host's own ""git config"" values.

  In-container the bridge writes them into git's **config-env**
  (""GIT_CONFIG_KEY_n"" / ""VALUE_n"") rather than a file, so a config read
  resolves without writing anywhere — and an identity the repo already
  carries is left alone, because a local ""\.git/config"" is a deliberate
  choice by whoever made it.
end note


@enduml
